---
import AppleIcon from "./AppleIcon.astro";
---

<header class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="halo">
      <img class="mark" src="/assets/icon.png" alt="ReelsEasy" width="112" height="112">
      <span class="aura" aria-hidden="true"><b></b><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
    </div>
    <p class="kicker">
      <AppleIcon />
      Reel editor for macOS, free and open source
    </p>
    <h1><span class="w" style="--i:0">I</span> <span class="w" style="--i:1">know</span> <span class="w" style="--i:2">you</span> <span class="w" style="--i:3">hate</span> <span class="w" style="--i:4">cutting</span> <span class="w" style="--i:5">clips.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">I hate it too. So I built a free, open source Mac app that does it for you.</p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn" href="#" data-download>
        <AppleIcon />
        Download for Mac
      </a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/Alexfrompixel/reelseasy">View on GitHub</a>
    </div>
    <p class="soon">The download isn't ready yet. If you're a developer, you can already <a href="https://github.com/Alexfrompixel/reelseasy#set-it-up">build it from the source</a>.</p>
    <div class="belt">
      <ul class="tags">
        <li>Cuts the pauses</li><li>Word-by-word captions</li><li>Zooms</li><li>Emojis</li><li>Sound effects</li><li>Transitions</li><li>Glitch and VHS</li><li>B-roll</li><li>1080x1920 export</li><li>Works with Claude and ChatGPT</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="stage">
      <div class="window">
        <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>ReelsEasy</span></div>
        <img src="/assets/app-editor.jpg" width="2400" height="1570" alt="The ReelsEasy editor: a vertical clip with captions and a second clip in the corner, above a timeline of cut pieces, captions, effects and sounds">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>
